# Failing-first tests, measured on upstream-lean base 1342059c and on this branch at load above 100 (agent-config .agent-config-4s70r). All four are red on base and green here; (a) and (b) ran here with the backlog and bead read bounds raised to 180s, because the 10s default expired under that load.
# (a) test_released_open_bead_tears_down_and_frees_its_tree in the bead-gate group of tests/fm-teardown.test.sh: a released open-bead task tears down and frees its tree; on base every open bead refuses.
# (b) test_unreleased_open_bead_still_refuses in the bead-gate group of tests/fm-teardown.test.sh: an unreleased open bead refuses, even with --force, the refusal names the release sentence, and an owner comment that quotes, conditions, or negates the sentence releases nothing, on any line and in what follows it; test_release_counts_only_as_the_owners_own_statement in the same group runs the full list of accepted and rejected texts through the bead read. On base the refusal names no release and no comment releases.
# (c) test_restore_brings_an_owner_released_task_back_on_a_fresh_tree in the restore group of tests/fm-control-relaunch.test.sh: relaunch --restore brings the archived task back on a fresh tree; on base the teardown before the restore refuses.
# (d) test_short_project_lock_holds_still_let_teardown_return_its_tree in tests/fm-teardown-endpoint-safety.test.sh: a dispatch holds the Treehouse project lock in short repeated holds and teardown still returns its tree within TEARDOWN_LOCK_WAIT_SECS. The first hold lasts until teardown's wait has polled, so a single try always meets it. Run as committed at load above 300: base refused with the project-lock error in 3 of 3 runs, and this branch returned its tree in 3 of 3 runs.
# The release-wording cases added for a hedged signature and for pending, provided, as soon as and waiting in the Checked note are red on this branch's earlier head 67236001 and green at c15eb815, where the bead-gate, restore and endpoint-safety groups all pass on upstream-lean c7e7f78a.
pr: 212
